<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Product recommendations</h2>
<p>Hold the product recommendations launch until consent is documented per app and purchase events suppress product recommendations promos immediately after checkout — both verifiable in an audit. In product recommendations, mistimed sends after purchases, refunds, or support cases destroy channel value quicker than any creative miss.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>No product recommendations promos without proof; transactional messages only</td><td>Consent evidence underwrites all product recommendations sending</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Product Recommendations education and proof before any offer</td><td>First-touch product recommendations codes create discount dependence</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Product Recommendations reminder with product context; discount withheld</td><td>Protects product recommendations profit when purchase intent is hottest</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Suppress product recommendations selling after checkout; educate instead</td><td>Keeps product recommendations buyers from instant list fatigue</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Hold product recommendations marketing while service cases stay open</td><td>Product Recommendations messaging lands badly during open cases</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Prune unengaged product recommendations profiles early</td><td>Product Recommendations inboxing survives on timely sunsets</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Hold product recommendations texts to quiet hours and frequency limits</td><td>Product Recommendations SMS risk exceeds email per complaint</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Product Recommendations B2B routing stays account-specific</td><td>Product Recommendations contract buyers need separate rules</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Verify product recommendations throwaway addresses pre-journey</td><td>Low-grade product recommendations signups drag deliverability</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Product Recommendations QA profiles excluded from reporting</td><td>Product Recommendations reporting stays clean without test noise</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Treat product recommendations snoops under normal consent policy</td><td>Ad-hoc product recommendations exceptions break traceability</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Reconfirm product recommendations consent where timestamps are missing</td><td>Product Recommendations compliance demands re-permission</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
